      "note": "Reviewed the exploit receipt and call trace, exact native/token payouts, Delegator creation, VerusProof creation and historical runtime, the contracts[] storage layout, every successful upgrade-selector transaction sent to the Delegator from the VerusProof installation through the pre-exploit block, each upgrade transaction's state diff, the commit-pinned reproduction, Verus's incident explanation, and the VerusProof patch. The anchor calls Delegator.submitImports and delegates first to SubmitImports, then to VerusProof 0x5e8060ecbf415aa25f12c1d67fde832bd87dcfa1, where the crafted supplemental output passes checkExportAndTransfers/proveImports. The May 22 patch adds an explicit FLAG_SUPPLEMENTAL rejection in VerusProof. The 19,397-byte VerusProof runtime was created in transaction 0x39828f2c49653f8281d24c0e05d119b1353a749aada1f5455f79ce6d14880f9c and hashes to 0x42928a45ef4c9b3b03550c972a98d1e49cb944d676f0f548e83c9920e8fb8dee from creation through the incident. Transaction 0x1de7078bb3ed60fe4d252f07af1a6d0003d1fc50772dbc86c7c05e4a83f91cb6 installed it in contracts[2]. The six later successful upgrade-selector calls changed other module slots; prestateTracer diffs show none wrote contracts[2], which still selected this artifact immediately before exploitation."
